craftinginfo-woodworking-text:
Raw wood is worked at several stations.

A <a href="handbook://block-immersivewoodworking:choppingblock">chopping block</a> splits wood with an axe, a log at a time.

A half-log is also a building block: place it with <hk>rightmouse</hk> and it becomes a half-log slab, split side out.

Beach driftwood is broken apart by hand: hold <hk>rightmouse</hk> to snap it into firewood and sticks, and larger pieces give more.

A pair of <a href="handbook://block-immersivewoodworking:sawhorse">sawhorses</a> rips a log lengthwise with a saw, into planks or support beams as you choose (<hk>toolmode</hk>).

The same sawhorses also strip bark: stand at the side and hold <hk>rightmouse</hk> with a <a href="handbook://item-immersivewoodworking:barkspud-copper">bark spud</a> or an axe with a hammer in the offhand.

